{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415513-how-does-the-knack-damage-conversion-work","id":1415513,"title":"How does the knack Damage Conversion work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-26T00:44:46-07:00","id":1415513,"title":"How does the knack Damage Conversion work?","content":"In Hero it says:<br /> &lt;blockquote&gt;<span style=\"font-family:serif\">Damage Conversion:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> When you administer medical </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">attention to a patient or yourself as an action, convert </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">any Injuries one lower: Maimed becomes Injured, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Injured becomes Bruised, and Bruised injuries heal </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">completely.&lt;/blockquote&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Does this take effect when you administer aid? Is there a limit to it's use (like once per character per session?). I'm asking because it seems to be a knack that is supposed to be used outside of combat as it seems generally just better than Combat Medic otherwise, thanks for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26245-nutsupial","name":"Nutsupial","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T07:08:11-07:00","id":1415819,"title":"","content":"I read Damage Conversion as applicable when using first aid, which is written as only being done outside of combat. You can only downgrade an injury condition once, so it only applies the one time. Also, Combat Medic can repair hard armor, which Damage Conversion cannot do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T23:46:20-07:00","id":1416062,"title":"","content":"This is my interpretation... it's written with several ambiguous phrases, so I can only say &quot;fair enough&quot; if someone else's interpretation doesn't match my own...<br /> <br /> Using the Knack strictly as written, whenever you take an action to &quot;administer medical attention&quot; you can convert all of their injuries a level lower. Barring additional Knacks, Boons, or other magic, most characters only have one basic action to administer medical attention - first aid, which can apply outside of combat, once per injury condition, and at most once per session. So at it's most basic level, it means you can reduce all of someone's injury conditions once per session while out of combat, rather than reducing one injury condition once per session.<br /> <br /> But, since it just needs to come into play whenever you're taking an action to &quot;administer medical attention&quot;, not just explicitly first aid, and additionally doesn't qualify between simple, reflexive, or out-of-combat actions, most Healer Knacks, Health Boons, and the Fertility innate power all seem like they qualify with a read-as-written interpretation. So, if you've got a power like Combat Medic or Doctor's Kit, in addition to the listed effect whatever you would normally get, you also get the benefits of Damage Conversion. Taking it in combination with another damage related Healer Knack makes you really, really good at combat healing.<br /> <br /> Note that this is all my RAW interpretation, not RAI. I have no ability to gauge the author's intent, so I can't really speak to intention. Healer has a number of issues, so I wouldn't be surprised if this is an unintended synergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}